  "visualReview": {
    "approach": "Individual full-size browser images were opened for all 31 element families and both foundations. Light and dark representative variants were inspected separately. All 79 fixtures were automatically checked at full and declared minimum slots in both modes.",
    "rounds": [
      {
        "round": 1,
        "finding": "Minimum-slot text exceeded five element families: agenda, architecture, list, vertical steps and vertical timeline.",
        "fix": "Reduced type by defined steps, reduced tokenized gaps, and suppressed timeline kickers at compact heights."
      },
      {
        "round": 2,
        "finding": "Inline surfaces stretched excessively in full slots; nested metric figures were too small; three-set Venn labels were obscured; hierarchy subtrees and mixed flowchart directions needed explicit connectors.",
        "fix": "Bound pill/tag/callout heights, strengthened nested figures, repositioned Venn sets and labels, and completed diagram wires."
      },
      {
        "round": 3,
        "finding": "Neutral preview CSS shared the frame class and small tag, affecting the picture frame size and number unit colors. The light accent-soft combination had 4.44 contrast.",
        "fix": "Scoped frame dimensions, explicitly inherited figure unit color, and lightened accent-soft for 4.552 contrast. Final font loading was awaited explicitly before capture."
      }
    ],
    "primaryIntegration": "Checked representative light/dark cards, line chart, hub, flowchart and table individually. Removed surplus filled shadow behind mixed-direction flowchart branches; both affected fixtures rerendered in both modes at full/min sizes without overflow."
  },
  "designDecisions": [
    "One integrated collection combines the five reference decks: thin frames and rules, restrained corner radii, teal hierarchy and blue/red/yellow supporting tones.",
    "The dark palette is independently designed around deep teal surfaces and pale accents, rather than mechanically inverted.",
    "No reference image is used as a rendered slide background. Photograph, logo and portrait material is represented by numbered neutral seats.",
    "The line chart uses CSS Anchor Positioning to connect values directly. Radial diagrams use CSS trigonometry and real directional connectors.",
    "Korean business fixture copy is newly written where the low-resolution reference did not define an element. English descriptions document the appearance only."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The pure CSS line-chart connection requires a browser supporting CSS Anchor Positioning; it was verified in the delivered Chromium environment.",
    "The collection interprets a shared design language across five source families; direct slide replication remains in the separate clone application."
  ],
